WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:11.719
Anti-cancer immune response can be conceptualized
as a series of stepwise events referred to

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:12.731
as the Cancer-Immunity Cycle.

00:00:12.731 --> 00:00:21.350
The cycle include: Step 1, release of cancer
cell antigens; Step 2, cancer antigen presentation;

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:28.230
Step 3, priming and activation; Step 4, trafficking
of immune cells to tumors; Step 5, infiltration

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:35.739
of immune cells into tumors; Step 6, recognition
of cancer cells by T cells; and Step 7, killing

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:36.949
of cancer cells.

00:00:36.949 --> 00:00:42.230
In this exercise, we will profile the status
of anti-cancer immunity across seven-step

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.830
of Cancer-Immunity Cycle, and infer the proportion
of various tumor-infiltrating immune cells

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.540
using the Tracking Tumor Immunophenotype,
or TIP web-based tool.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.800
The TIP is a meta-server which integrates
systematically two existing third party methods

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.989
for tracking, analyzing and visualizing the
status of anti-cancer immunity. and the proportion

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:01.120
of tumor-infiltrating immune cells across
seven-step of Cancer-Immunity Cycle using

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.120
transcriptomic data.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.120
To start with the immunotype profiling, we
will first need to cleanup the transcriptomic

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.120
dataset.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.619
Note, for the dataset to be uploaded to the
TIP, there should be no missing values within

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:09.560
the table, and no duplication of gene ID.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:29.140
To prepare the dataset, we will first remove
the unnamed gene ID.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:02:16.480
Next, we will remove the columns with zero
read count.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:03:04.970
And finally, we will remove any duplicated
gene ID.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:04:03.050
Once the dataset is cleaned up.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:05:15.360
We will save it as a separate TSV file.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:48.190
Now, we will upload the file onto the TIP
tool.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:06:00.899
Once the analysis is done, you can export
the results for further analysis.

